\begin{proof}
Apply the local assertion of Lemma~\ref{p1:arith:defects}
with $H=10B$ to $V_x$.
In the critical band its diameter is $O(B)$ and its values
lie in $[N/2,3N]$ for all sufficiently large $N$.
The comparison constants are uniform in $x$.
\end{proof}

Proposition~\ref{p1:discussion:charlier-norm} gives
$\|\Pi_1*\Delta^{*2}\|_1=3/e$, hence $\mathcal C(1)=3/(4e)$.
Along $N=2^L$ with $3\mid L$, the pair coefficient therefore gives
\begin{equation}
 \TV(\Law Z_N,\Pi_1)
       \sim \frac1{12e}\,L N^{-2/3}.
 \label{p1:close:dyadic-example}
\end{equation}
This is the coefficient in the example announced in the introduction.
